Applies to: **the research record** — class 2 of the file-level licensing policy in
`LICENSE`. Concretely: every `.md` file in this repository (`docs/`, `README.md`,
`CONTRIBUTING.md`, `SECURITY.md`, the case-study and engine write-ups in `engines/` and
`agents/`, `results/README.md` and each dataset `README.md`), every `.tsv` record extract
under `results/`, every `manifest.json` under `results/`, and any table, figure, finding,
evidence classification or derived analysis published alongside them.

It does **not** apply to the executable source files of class 1 (`scripts/`, `tests/`,
`results/strata/*/extract.awk`, `.github/workflows/`, `.gitignore`), which are MIT, nor to
the two license files themselves, which are scope-neutral. The full rule, the enumerated
file list and the SPDX marker requirement are in `LICENSE` §"Scope of this file".

Research commentary belongs to this license even when it used to sit inside a source
file: on 2026-11-05 the historical and analytical commentary in the `extract.awk` headers
was moved into the dataset `README.md` beside each program, so that the MIT-class files
carry only operational comments. See `docs/evidence-inventory.md` §6.2.

